.TH RECOIL16 7 "2026-09-25" "recoil16" "recoil16"
.SH NAME
recoil16 \- drivers and tools for the PCSpecialist Recoil 16 AMD (TUXEDO Stellaris 16 Gen7)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The recoil16 package builds four kernel modules with DKMS and installs
\fBrecoil16ctl\fR(1) to control them:
.TP
.B uniwill-laptop
Fn keys (keyboard backlight, Sc), firmware power modes as a platform profile,
battery charge modes and health, Fn lock, Super-key lock, fan and temperature sensors.
Replaces the stock module; needs kernel 7.2 or newer.
.TP
.B ite8291-mono
Keyboard backlight (white, 0\-50), as \fI/sys/class/leds/ite8291:white:kbd_backlight\fR.
.TP
.B ite8233-lightbar
RGB lightbar, as \fI/sys/class/leds/rgb:lightbar\fR.
.TP
.B copilot-rctrl
Turns the Copilot key back into Right Ctrl (an i8042 filter; no virtual input device).
.PP
On kernels older than 7.2 (for example a 6.18 LTS fallback) only
\fBite8291-mono\fR, \fBite8233-lightbar\fR and \fBcopilot-rctrl\fR are built.
.SH SETUP
.TP
.B Check
Run \fBrecoil16ctl check\fR after installing, after upgrades and after kernel
updates. It checks the kernel, modules, DKMS, charge mode, power profile,
keyboard, lightbar, Copilot filter, sensors and the Sc shortcut, and lists the
checks that need a person.
.TP
.B Charge mode
\fBsudo recoil16ctl battery mode\fR \fBstandard\fR|\fBlong-life\fR|\fBtrickle\fR
charges fully, to about 93% or to about 90%. The embedded controller lowers
the charge voltage and still reports 100% / Full. It forgets the mode at
shutdown, so the command also writes a udev rule that re-applies it whenever
the driver loads. The 1.0.0 percentage limit was removed: it may damage the
battery on this model.
.TP
.B Battery health
\fBrecoil16ctl battery status\fR shows the learned battery health and cycle
count read from the embedded controller; the firmware reports design capacity
and 0 cycles to the OS until 50 cycles.
.TP
.B Sc key (KDE Plasma)
Rotates the screen 180\(de from the first login after installing. The default
shortcut is listed as \fIRecoil 16 \(-> Rotate Screen 180\(de\fR in
System Settings \(-> Keyboard \(-> Shortcuts, where it can be changed. Remove any
Sc shortcut bound by hand earlier, otherwise the two clash.
.TP
.B Lightbar
Off at boot until set, for example with \fBsudo recoil16ctl lightbar blue 60\fR;
the setting is saved and applied at every boot.
.TP
.B Power modes
The mode button next to the power button, the desktop power slider and
\fBrecoil16ctl profile\fR all switch the same firmware mode:
low-power (office, green), balanced (balance, blue), performance (turbo, purple).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/90-recoil16-charge-mode.rules
Re-applies the charge mode when the driver binds. Written by
\fBrecoil16ctl battery mode\fR, removed by \fBrecoil16ctl battery clear-rule\fR
(which also removes a 1.0.0 \fI90-recoil16-charge-limit.rules\fR).
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/ite8233-lightbar.conf
Lightbar colour and brightness at boot. Written by \fBrecoil16ctl lightbar\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kglobalaccel/recoil16.desktop
KDE default global shortcut: Sc runs \fBrecoil16ctl screen rotate\fR.
.TP
.I /usr/src/recoil16-VERSION/
Module sources for DKMS.
.SH REMOVAL
With the Arch package: \fBsudo pacman \-R recoil16-dkms\fR (or \fBrecoil16-dkms-git\fR), then reboot.
With the install script: \fBsudo scripts/uninstall.sh\fR from the source tree,
then reboot. Both remove the charge-mode boot rule; the embedded controller
is back to Standard after the reboot.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
DKMS build fails
Install the headers for the running kernel; the build log is
\fI/var/lib/dkms/recoil16/VERSION/build/make.log\fR.
.TP
"Missing VERSION kernel headers" from the DKMS pacman hook
A leftover \fI/usr/lib/modules/VERSION\fR of a removed kernel. If
\fBpacman \-Qo\fR says no package owns it, delete it.
.TP
Nothing works after boot
\fBmodinfo \-F filename uniwill-laptop\fR shows the stock module instead of
\fI.../updates/dkms/...\fR: run \fBsudo depmod \-a\fR and reboot.
.TP
recoil16ctl completion does not work in zsh
The completion cache predates the install: \fBrm ~/.zcompdump*\fR and open a new shell.
.TP
KDE's power daemon crashed after loading the modules by hand
PowerDevil 6.7 crashes on a keyboard brightness key if the backlight appeared
after login: \fBsystemctl \-\-user restart plasma-powerdevil\fR.
.TP
copilot-rctrl: "cannot install i8042 filter"
Another driver owns the i8042 filter; find it with \fBlsmod\fR and \fBdmesg\fR.
.TP
"permission denied ... run with sudo"
Changing settings needs root; reading them does not.
.TP
"run 'recoil16ctl screen' as your desktop user"
Screen rotation talks to the user's KDE session; run it without sudo.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrecoil16ctl\fR(1), \fBrecoil16ctl\-check\fR(1), \fBdkms\fR(8),
\fBpowerprofilesctl\fR(1)
.PP
Source, installation on other distributions and upstream patches:
\fIhttps://github.com/amad3v/recoil16\fR
